"""Real companies for the shipper and consignee on each air waybill, matched to the cargo and to where it flies.

Every entry is a real organization that does this kind of business in the places it's tagged with:
  "US"   a country (ISO code, as in airports.json)
  "@EU"  a region: @NA @SA @EU @AF @AS @OC @ME (Middle East, see shipments.ME)
  "*"    anywhere (global companies, used when nothing local fits)

The shipments themselves are fictional, made for flight simulation; the paperwork says so and no business
relationship with PAC is implied. "{city}" is filled with the airport's city.
"""
